      en: ["UNESCO World Heritage site designated in 1996.", "Shared across Burkina Faso, Benin, and Niger.", "Named after a prominent W-shaped bend in the Niger River.", "Central part of the W-Arly-Pendjari (WAP) Complex.", "Hosts the last significant population of West African lions.", "Expanded by UNESCO in 2017 to cover a larger area."],
